.TH SENTRYLAB 1 "October 2026" "SentryLab 1.1.1"
.SH NAME
sentrylab \- publish PVE CPU and disk temperatures to MQTT
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sentrylab
.RB [ --config " file" ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
SentryLab reads Intel/AMD CPU and NVMe/hwmon disk temperatures and publishes
Home Assistant MQTT discovery. Optional SMART queries skip standby disks.
The package installs a systemd timer that runs once per minute.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B configure
Interactively save MQTT credentials. Password input is hidden.
Enable the timer and publish an initial sample when systemd is running.
.TP
.B check
Print collected temperatures without connecting to MQTT.
Optional SMART collection can still access awake disks.
.TP
.B run
Publish one sample and retained discovery configurations.
.TP
.B ready
Exit successfully only when MQTT publishing is configured and enabled.
Used by the systemd service condition.
.TP
.B cleanup
Delete retained discovery entries recorded by this installation.
Run before changing brokers when the old broker should be cleaned up.
.TP
.B enable
Enable and start the systemd timer.
.TP
.B disable
Disable the timer and stop the current collection service.
.TP
.B status
Show the timer status.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sentrylab/sentrylab.conf
INI configuration; root-readable only. Preserved on upgrade and removal.
.TP
.I /var/lib/sentrylab/
Private MQTT discovery manifest and operation lock.
.SH REMOVAL
Use apt remove sentrylab-pve to keep configuration, or apt purge sentrylab-pve
to remove configuration and state. MQTT cleanup is best effort when offline.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR smartctl (8)
